{%- comment -%}
  ca-theme-variables.liquid — Conspire Agency custom CSS variables.

  Use this for :root variables that need Liquid (e.g. values pulled from theme
  settings), which plain CSS in ca-custom.css cannot do. For static values or
  simple overrides of Shopify's variables, prefer ca-custom.css instead.

  Rendered from ca-head.liquid, after Shopify's theme-styles-variables, so these
  override the theme's values.

  Example:
    :root {
      --ca-brand-accent: {{ settings.color_accent | default: '#ff5a1f' }};
    }
{%- endcomment -%}

{% style %}
  :root {
    /* Add Liquid-driven custom variables here */
  }
{% endstyle %}
